                  Setup commands used in the USERTYPE
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you set up different ratio's for all your conferences, then your setup of
a usertype must be made in the correct order.
You must do it this way:
All ratio/dlbyte/ulbyte settings for a conference must be SET before you
specify the conference name/number.






CONF                     (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Conference number that a user got access to.
                                  same as below but the number of the
                                  conference, not name.

CONFERENCE               (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Conference name that a user got access to.

DLDAYLIMIT               (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select maximum download bytes per day.
                                  in current conference.

DOWNLOADFILES            (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of files user will start
                                  to have downloaded when he logs into current
                                  conference the first time.

DOWNLOADBYTES            (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of bytes user will start
                                  to have uploaded when he logs into current
                                  conference the first time.

RATIO                    (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select RATIO for current usertype
                                  in current conference

RATIOTYPE                (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Select RATIOTYPE for usertype
                                  in current conference
                                  You can choose between 4 different ratiotypes
                                  for a user:
                                   DISABLED      : User got freedown
                                                   He do not need to upload
                                                   before download

                                   BYTES         : Users upload bytes
                                                   will be compared using
                                                   selected ratio and
                                                   if he do not have enough
                                                   bytes left, he will not
                                                   be able to download.

                                   FILES         : Users upload files
                                                   will be compared using
                                                   selected ratio and
                                                   if he do not have enough
                                                   files left, he will not
                                                   be able to download.

                                   FILES&BYTES   : User got both files and
                                                   bytes ratio, both will be
                                                   checked when he tries to
                                                   download.

UPLOADFILES              (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of files user will start
                                  to have uploaded when he logs into current
                                  conference the first time.

UPLOADBYTES              (pn)   : DEFAULT: 0
                                : select number of bytes user will start
                                  to have uploaded when he logs into current
                                  conference the first time.
